{"authored" [{"question" "q-74403" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$\\int (3{cos}^{2}⁡x+1-3{sin}^{2}⁡x)\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040629/state.json" "file_sha256" "c9c104bfd85793ef3e6d6c2ccc5bf90e923f876ab7a0df3bc4c1c9aae75799f1" "basis" 1458 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040629/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-74403" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We can use the double-angle formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta -{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta =\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta \n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (3{cos}^{2}⁡x+1-3{sin}^{2}⁡x)\\text{d}x & =\\int [3({cos}^{2}⁡x-{sin}^{2}⁡x)+1]\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (3\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+1)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3(\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡2x)+x+C \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040629/state.json" "file_sha256" "c9c104bfd85793ef3e6d6c2ccc5bf90e923f876ab7a0df3bc4c1c9aae75799f1" "basis" 1458 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040629/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-74403" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040629/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8952b286a033e30dac12d7f47bfda0bf8abe50ab1981d82fa9faa37531b2bbe4" "basis" 1458 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040629/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-74403" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040629/state.json" "file_sha256" "c9c104bfd85793ef3e6d6c2ccc5bf90e923f876ab7a0df3bc4c1c9aae75799f1" "basis" 1458 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040629/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-74403" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+x+C"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040629/state.json" "file_sha256" "c9c104bfd85793ef3e6d6c2ccc5bf90e923f876ab7a0df3bc4c1c9aae75799f1" "basis" 1458 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040629/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-74403" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+x+C"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040629/state.json" "file_sha256" "c9c104bfd85793ef3e6d6c2ccc5bf90e923f876ab7a0df3bc4c1c9aae75799f1" "basis" 1458 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040629/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-74403" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "3\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+1+C"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040629/state.json" "file_sha256" "c9c104bfd85793ef3e6d6c2ccc5bf90e923f876ab7a0df3bc4c1c9aae75799f1" "basis" 1458 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040629/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-74403" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+1+C"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040629/state.json" "file_sha256" "c9c104bfd85793ef3e6d6c2ccc5bf90e923f876ab7a0df3bc4c1c9aae75799f1" "basis" 1458 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040629/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-74403" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+x+C"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040629/state.json" "file_sha256" "c9c104bfd85793ef3e6d6c2ccc5bf90e923f876ab7a0df3bc4c1c9aae75799f1" "basis" 1458 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040629/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-74403" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+x+C"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040629/state.json" "file_sha256" "c9c104bfd85793ef3e6d6c2ccc5bf90e923f876ab7a0df3bc4c1c9aae75799f1" "basis" 1458 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040629/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-348724" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /2}(2{cos}^{2}⁡3x-2{sin}^{2}⁡3x+6x)\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040629/state.json" "file_sha256" "c9c104bfd85793ef3e6d6c2ccc5bf90e923f876ab7a0df3bc4c1c9aae75799f1" "basis" 1458 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040629/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-348724" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Here, we use the double-angle formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta ={cos}^{2}⁡\\theta -{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nLetting $\\theta =3x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡6x={cos}^{2}⁡3x-{sin}^{2}⁡3x.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into our integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /2}(2{cos}^{2}⁡3x-2{sin}^{2}⁡3x+6x)\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /2}(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡6x+6x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={(\\frac{2}{6}\\operatorname{sin}⁡6x+\\frac{6}{2}{x}^{2})|}_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & ={(\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡6x+3{x}^{2})|}_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =[\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\pi )+3{(\\frac{\\pi }{2})}^{2}]-[\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi )+3{(\\frac{\\pi }{6})}^{2}] \\\\  & =3(\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{4}-\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{36}) \\\\  & =\\frac{2{\\pi }^{2}}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040629/state.json" "file_sha256" "c9c104bfd85793ef3e6d6c2ccc5bf90e923f876ab7a0df3bc4c1c9aae75799f1" "basis" 1458 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040629/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-348724" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040629/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8952b286a033e30dac12d7f47bfda0bf8abe50ab1981d82fa9faa37531b2bbe4" "basis" 1458 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040629/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-348724" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040629/state.json" "file_sha256" "c9c104bfd85793ef3e6d6c2ccc5bf90e923f876ab7a0df3bc4c1c9aae75799f1" "basis" 1458 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040629/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-361711" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/assets/f8aa97ff1ff27ec11df6aefd4523ed9d39efac686c777f7242701aa2f4fef79c.png)\n\nA region in the $xy$-plane is bounded by the curve $y=2{cos}^{2}⁡(2x)+2-x,$ the $x$-axis and the lines $x=0$ and $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$, as shown above. The area of the region is\n\n$A=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/state.json" "file_sha256" "7abfce496194bab47d4728ee1b0aae97d930870b97a49488d63b011f30d2c06a" "basis" 1379 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-361711" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The area of the region is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}(2{cos}^{2}⁡(2x)+2-x)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo calculate this integral, we use the double-angle formula for cosine that involves the ${cos}^{2}⁡x$ term, given by\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x=2{cos}^{2}⁡x-1.\n$$\n\n \n\nRearranging, we have\n\n$$\n{cos}^{2}⁡x=\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+1).\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into our integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}(2{cos}^{2}⁡(2x)+2-x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}[(\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+1)+2-x]\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+3-x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={(\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x+3x-\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2})|}_{0}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =[\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\pi )+3\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{2}-\\frac{1}{2}{(\\frac{\\pi }{2})}^{2}]-[\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0)+3(0)-\\frac{1}{2}(0)^{2}] \\\\  & =[\\frac{3\\pi }{2}-\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{8}]-[0] \\\\  & =\\frac{12\\pi -{\\pi }^{2}}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/state.json" "file_sha256" "7abfce496194bab47d4728ee1b0aae97d930870b97a49488d63b011f30d2c06a" "basis" 1379 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-361711" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "368a25e897701508920ebc2380c176850dc903b2f623629d4ed9b2dfbce80cfb" "basis" 1379 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-361711" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/state.json" "file_sha256" "7abfce496194bab47d4728ee1b0aae97d930870b97a49488d63b011f30d2c06a" "basis" 1379 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-347182" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }(2{cos}^{2}⁡(4x)-{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/state.json" "file_sha256" "7abfce496194bab47d4728ee1b0aae97d930870b97a49488d63b011f30d2c06a" "basis" 1379 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-347182" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Here, we use the double-angle formula for cosine that involves the ${cos}^{2}⁡\\theta $ term, given by\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta =2{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta -1.\n$$\n\n \n\nRearranging, we have\n\n$$\n2{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta =\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta +1.\n$$\n\nLetting $\\theta =4x,$ we have\n\n$$\n2{cos}^{2}⁡(4x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(8x)+1.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into our integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }(2{cos}^{2}⁡(4x)-{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(8x)+1-{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(\\frac{1}{8}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(8x)+x-\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3})\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =(\\frac{1}{8}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(8\\pi )+\\pi -\\frac{1}{3}{\\pi }^{3})-(\\frac{1}{8}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0)+0-\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot {0}^{3}) \\\\  & =\\pi -\\frac{{\\pi }^{3}}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\pi -{\\pi }^{3}}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi (3-{\\pi }^{2})}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/state.json" "file_sha256" "7abfce496194bab47d4728ee1b0aae97d930870b97a49488d63b011f30d2c06a" "basis" 1379 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-347182" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "368a25e897701508920ebc2380c176850dc903b2f623629d4ed9b2dfbce80cfb" "basis" 1379 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-347182" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/state.json" "file_sha256" "7abfce496194bab47d4728ee1b0aae97d930870b97a49488d63b011f30d2c06a" "basis" 1379 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-347182" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\pi-\\frac{\\pi^3}{3}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/state.json" "file_sha256" "7abfce496194bab47d4728ee1b0aae97d930870b97a49488d63b011f30d2c06a" "basis" 1379 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/edb-import/verification.json"}] "sources" [{"question" "q-49286" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040941/assets/0f8e4dc1dff5673d8fc95375f9632f43bc4942335899e0e6dad11e8693bd6599.png)\n\nA region in the $xy$-plane is bounded by the curve $y=5{sin}^{2}⁡x,$ the $x$-axis and the lines $x=0$ and $x=\\pi .$ The area of the region is" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040941/state.json" "file_sha256" "744314f6ad730bd0ae63a2eaa79c1f39557d61321b70bfb1342766d564cd0eff"} {"question" "q-49286" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The area of the region bounded by the curve $y=5{sin}^{2}⁡x,$ the $x$-axis and the lines $x=0$ and $x=\\pi $ is \n\n$$\nA={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }5{sin}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nLet's recall the double-angle formula for cosine that involves the ${sin}^{2}$ term: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x=1-2{sin}^{2}⁡x\n$$\n\nWe can rearrange the above formula as\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{2}(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x)={sin}^{2}⁡x.\n$$\n\nWe can now integrate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }5{sin}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =5{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{sin}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =5{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\frac{1}{2}(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}{(x-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x)|}_{0}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}([\\pi -\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\pi )]-[0-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot 0)]) \\\\  & =\\frac{5\\pi }{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040941/state.json" "file_sha256" "744314f6ad730bd0ae63a2eaa79c1f39557d61321b70bfb1342766d564cd0eff"} {"question" "q-49286" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040941/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a56cd9bf1d57c2cd96862431dd8f9d442af99ac3c07b3d2d6a08e1478ca83919"} {"question" "q-49286" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040941/state.json" "file_sha256" "744314f6ad730bd0ae63a2eaa79c1f39557d61321b70bfb1342766d564cd0eff"} {"question" "q-49286" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2\\pi "] ["math" "\\frac{3\\pi }{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{5\\pi }{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\pi }{2}"] ["math" "\\pi "]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040941/state.json" "file_sha256" "744314f6ad730bd0ae63a2eaa79c1f39557d61321b70bfb1342766d564cd0eff"} {"question" "q-49286" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{5\\pi }{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040941/state.json" "file_sha256" "744314f6ad730bd0ae63a2eaa79c1f39557d61321b70bfb1342766d564cd0eff"} {"question" "q-74403" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$\\int (3{cos}^{2}⁡x+1-3{sin}^{2}⁡x)\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040941/state.json" "file_sha256" "744314f6ad730bd0ae63a2eaa79c1f39557d61321b70bfb1342766d564cd0eff"} {"question" "q-74403" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We can use the double-angle formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta -{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta =\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta \n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (3{cos}^{2}⁡x+1-3{sin}^{2}⁡x)\\text{d}x & =\\int [3({cos}^{2}⁡x-{sin}^{2}⁡x)+1]\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (3\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+1)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3(\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡2x)+x+C \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040941/state.json" "file_sha256" "744314f6ad730bd0ae63a2eaa79c1f39557d61321b70bfb1342766d564cd0eff"} {"question" "q-74403" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040941/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a56cd9bf1d57c2cd96862431dd8f9d442af99ac3c07b3d2d6a08e1478ca83919"} {"question" "q-74403" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040941/state.json" "file_sha256" "744314f6ad730bd0ae63a2eaa79c1f39557d61321b70bfb1342766d564cd0eff"} {"question" "q-74403" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+x+C"] ["math" "-\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+x+C"] ["math" "3\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+1+C"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+1+C"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+x+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040941/state.json" "file_sha256" "744314f6ad730bd0ae63a2eaa79c1f39557d61321b70bfb1342766d564cd0eff"} {"question" "q-74403" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+x+C"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040941/state.json" "file_sha256" "744314f6ad730bd0ae63a2eaa79c1f39557d61321b70bfb1342766d564cd0eff"} {"question" "q-347182" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }(2{cos}^{2}⁡(4x)-{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040941/state.json" "file_sha256" "744314f6ad730bd0ae63a2eaa79c1f39557d61321b70bfb1342766d564cd0eff"} {"question" "q-347182" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Here, we use the double-angle formula for cosine that involves the ${cos}^{2}⁡\\theta $ term, given by\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta =2{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta -1.\n$$\n\n \n\nRearranging, we have\n\n$$\n2{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta =\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta +1.\n$$\n\nLetting $\\theta =4x,$ we have\n\n$$\n2{cos}^{2}⁡(4x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(8x)+1.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into our integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }(2{cos}^{2}⁡(4x)-{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(8x)+1-{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(\\frac{1}{8}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(8x)+x-\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3})\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =(\\frac{1}{8}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(8\\pi )+\\pi -\\frac{1}{3}{\\pi }^{3})-(\\frac{1}{8}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0)+0-\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot {0}^{3}) \\\\  & =\\pi -\\frac{{\\pi }^{3}}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\pi -{\\pi }^{3}}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi (3-{\\pi }^{2})}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040941/state.json" "file_sha256" "744314f6ad730bd0ae63a2eaa79c1f39557d61321b70bfb1342766d564cd0eff"} {"question" "q-347182" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040941/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a56cd9bf1d57c2cd96862431dd8f9d442af99ac3c07b3d2d6a08e1478ca83919"} {"question" "q-347182" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040941/state.json" "file_sha256" "744314f6ad730bd0ae63a2eaa79c1f39557d61321b70bfb1342766d564cd0eff"} {"question" "q-347182" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\pi-\\frac{\\pi^3}{3}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040941/state.json" "file_sha256" "744314f6ad730bd0ae63a2eaa79c1f39557d61321b70bfb1342766d564cd0eff"} {"question" "q-348724" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /2}(2{cos}^{2}⁡3x-2{sin}^{2}⁡3x+6x)\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040941/state.json" "file_sha256" "744314f6ad730bd0ae63a2eaa79c1f39557d61321b70bfb1342766d564cd0eff"} {"question" "q-348724" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Here, we use the double-angle formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta ={cos}^{2}⁡\\theta -{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nLetting $\\theta =3x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡6x={cos}^{2}⁡3x-{sin}^{2}⁡3x.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into our integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /2}(2{cos}^{2}⁡3x-2{sin}^{2}⁡3x+6x)\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /2}(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡6x+6x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={(\\frac{2}{6}\\operatorname{sin}⁡6x+\\frac{6}{2}{x}^{2})|}_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & ={(\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡6x+3{x}^{2})|}_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =[\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\pi )+3{(\\frac{\\pi }{2})}^{2}]-[\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi )+3{(\\frac{\\pi }{6})}^{2}] \\\\  & =3(\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{4}-\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{36}) \\\\  & =\\frac{2{\\pi }^{2}}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040941/state.json" "file_sha256" "744314f6ad730bd0ae63a2eaa79c1f39557d61321b70bfb1342766d564cd0eff"} {"question" "q-348724" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040941/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a56cd9bf1d57c2cd96862431dd8f9d442af99ac3c07b3d2d6a08e1478ca83919"} {"question" "q-348724" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040941/state.json" "file_sha256" "744314f6ad730bd0ae63a2eaa79c1f39557d61321b70bfb1342766d564cd0eff"} {"question" "q-348724" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{2\\pi^2}{3}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040941/state.json" "file_sha256" "744314f6ad730bd0ae63a2eaa79c1f39557d61321b70bfb1342766d564cd0eff"} {"question" "q-361711" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040941/assets/f8aa97ff1ff27ec11df6aefd4523ed9d39efac686c777f7242701aa2f4fef79c.png)\n\nA region in the $xy$-plane is bounded by the curve $y=2{cos}^{2}⁡(2x)+2-x,$ the $x$-axis and the lines $x=0$ and $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$, as shown above. The area of the region is\n\n$A=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040941/state.json" "file_sha256" "744314f6ad730bd0ae63a2eaa79c1f39557d61321b70bfb1342766d564cd0eff"} {"question" "q-361711" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The area of the region is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}(2{cos}^{2}⁡(2x)+2-x)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo calculate this integral, we use the double-angle formula for cosine that involves the ${cos}^{2}⁡x$ term, given by\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x=2{cos}^{2}⁡x-1.\n$$\n\n \n\nRearranging, we have\n\n$$\n{cos}^{2}⁡x=\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+1).\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into our integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}(2{cos}^{2}⁡(2x)+2-x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}[(\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+1)+2-x]\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+3-x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={(\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x+3x-\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2})|}_{0}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =[\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\pi )+3\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{2}-\\frac{1}{2}{(\\frac{\\pi }{2})}^{2}]-[\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0)+3(0)-\\frac{1}{2}(0)^{2}] \\\\  & =[\\frac{3\\pi }{2}-\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{8}]-[0] \\\\  & =\\frac{12\\pi -{\\pi }^{2}}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040941/state.json" "file_sha256" "744314f6ad730bd0ae63a2eaa79c1f39557d61321b70bfb1342766d564cd0eff"} {"question" "q-361711" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040941/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a56cd9bf1d57c2cd96862431dd8f9d442af99ac3c07b3d2d6a08e1478ca83919"} {"question" "q-361711" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040941/state.json" "file_sha256" "744314f6ad730bd0ae63a2eaa79c1f39557d61321b70bfb1342766d564cd0eff"} {"question" "q-361711" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{3\\pi}{2}-\\frac{\\pi^2}{8}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040941/state.json" "file_sha256" "744314f6ad730bd0ae63a2eaa79c1f39557d61321b70bfb1342766d564cd0eff"}] "usage" {"q-348724" [] "q-74403" [] "q-361711" [] "q-347182" []} "basis" 1468 "retractions" [[17592186303665 :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/assets/f8aa97ff1ff27ec11df6aefd4523ed9d39efac686c777f7242701aa2f4fef79c.png)\n\nA region in the $xy$-plane is bounded by the curve $y=2{cos}^{2}⁡(2x)+2-x,$ the $x$-axis and the lines $x=0$ and $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$, as shown above. T